FZUS73 KDLH 082236

MWSDLH



Marine Weather Statement

National Weather Service Duluth MN

536 PM CDT Fri Aug 8 2025



LSZ121-147-148-150-162-082330-

536 PM CDT Fri Aug 8 2025



...A STRONG THUNDERSTORM OVER THE WATERS...



The areas affected include...

  Chequamegon Bay-Bayfield to Oak Point WI...

  Lake Superior west of a line from Saxon Harbor WI to Grand Portage 

  MN beyond 5NM...

  Oak Point to Saxon Harbor WI...

  Outer Apostle Islands Beyond 5 NM from Mainland...

  Sand Island to Bayfield WI...



At 536 PM CDT, Doppler radar indicated a strong thunderstorm, capable

of producing winds to around 30 knots. This thunderstorm was located

near Madeline Island, moving east at 35 knots.



PRECAUTIONARY/PREPAREDNESS ACTIONS...



Mariners can expect gusty winds to around 30 knots, locally higher

waves, and lightning strikes. Boaters should seek safe harbor

immediately until this storm passes.



