Fire Weather Planning Forecast for Western Alaska

National Weather Service Fairbanks AK

237 PM AKDT Fri Aug 8 2025



.DISCUSSION...

Moderate to heavy rain is likely this afternoon through Sunday 

morning across Western Alaska. Expect a widespread 0.25 to 0.50" 

across the Western Interior and along the coast. Higher totals up 

to 1.00" are possible in the higher terrain of the Seward 

Peninsula, and from the Upper Kobuk Valley north. Another round of

rain, this time accompanied by strong south/southwest winds is 

expected Monday and Tuesday. Many areas may receive upwards of 1" 

of rain or more. Winds will be strongest along the coast, 

potentially gusting 40 to 50 mph, with 20 to 30 mph gusts inland. 

Temperatures will remain cool with highs largely in the 50s and 

60s. No significant fire weather danger is expected for the 

foreseeable future. 



