583

FNUS76 KLOX 082244

FWSLOX



Spot Forecast for Canyon Fire...LACoFD

National Weather Service Los Angeles/Oxnard CA

344 PM PDT Fri Aug 8 2025



If conditions become unrepresentative, contact the National Weather

Service.



.DISCUSSION...



Moderate to high confidence in a diurnal wind pattern, with fairly

light northeast/downcanyon winds in the overnight to early morning

hours, becoming upcanyon (southwest to southeast) during the 

afternoon and evening. Winds will decrease rapidly between 8PM and 

10PM each night. High temperatures will be within a couple degrees 

of each other each day, hottest at higher elevations, and minimum 

relative humidities will likely increase 1-2 percent each day. 

During the peak heating of the day, moderate plume-dominated fire 

behavior will be possible, mainly during the mid to late afternoon 

hours into early evening. Winds will turn northwest to north Sunday 

night.





.SATURDAY...



Sky/weather.........Sunny with areas of smoke. 

Max temperature.....91-96. 

Min humidity........18-22 percent. 

Eye level winds.....Downcanyon winds 1-3 mph through 9AM, becoming 

                    upcanyon 6-8 mph with gusts to 10 mph in the 

                    afternoon.

Wind (20 ft)........Downcanyon winds 3-5 mph through 9AM, becoming 

                    upcanyon 10-12 mph with gusts to 20 mph in the 

                    afternoon.

Ridgetop wind.......Northeast winds 3-6 mph becoming south-southwest 

                    12-15 mph with gusts to 22 mph in the afternoon. 

Mixing height.......800 ft AGL in the morning, increasing to 

                    4500-5500 ft AGL in the afternoon. 

Transport winds.....Light winds becoming southwest 10-15 mph 

                    with gusts to 25 mph in the afternoon. 





.SATURDAY NIGHT...



Sky/weather.........Clear. 

Min temperature.....65-75, coolest in the valleys. 

Max humidity........45-55 percent in the canyons, 35-45 percent 

                    in the hills. 

Eye level winds.....Upcanyon 4-6 mph with gusts to 10 mph through 

                    9PM, becoming downcanyon 2-4 mph.

Wind (20 ft)........Upcanyon 8-10 mph with gusts to 18 mph through 

                    9PM, becoming downcanyon 4-7 mph.

Ridgetop wind.......South-southwest 10 to 12 mph with gusts 20 mph 

                    through 9 PM, becoming north-northeast 4-7 mph 

Mixing height.......3500 ft AGL early, becoming 800 ft AGL. 

Transport winds.....Southwest 10 to 12 mph with gusts to 18 mph early, 

                    becoming northeast 1 to 5 mph. 



.SUNDAY...



Sky/weather.........Sunny. 

Max temperature.....92-97. 

Min humidity........20-25 percent

Eye level winds.....Downcanyon winds 2-4 mph through 9AM, becoming 

                    upcanyon 4-6 mph with gusts to 10 mph in the 

                    afternoon.

Wind (20 ft)........Downcanyon winds 4-8 mph through 9AM, becoming 

                    upcanyon 8-10 mph with gusts to 18 mph in the 

                    afternoon.

Ridgetop wind.......Northeast winds 3-6 mph becoming south-southwest 

                    10-12 mph with gusts to 20 mph in the afternoon. 

Mixing height.......800 ft AGL in the morning, increasing to 

                    4800-5800 ft AGL in the afternoon. 

Transport winds.....Northeast 1 to 5 mph becoming southwest 8-10 mph 

                    with gusts to 15 mph in the afternoon. 



$$

