Mount Rainier Recreational Forecast

National Weather Service Seattle WA

351 PM PDT Fri Aug 8 2025



.SYNOPSIS...Upper level ridging over Mount Rainier National Park

will maintain a dry and warmer pattern into early next week. 

The ridge will weaken on Tuesday and upper level troughing will 

settle over the area through late in the week, bringing cooler

temperatures and the chance of light precipitation Thursday into 

Friday.



&&



.FRIDAY NIGHT...Partly cloudy then becoming mostly cloudy in the

late evening and early morning then becoming partly cloudy.

Freezing level near 14500 feet. 

.SATURDAY...Mostly sunny. Freezing level near 15000 feet. 

.SATURDAY NIGHT...Mostly clear. Freezing level near 16500 feet. 

.SUNDAY...Sunny. Freezing level near 16500 feet. 



