982

FNAK53 PAFG 082258

FWFAFG



Fire Weather Planning Forecast for Interior Alaska

National Weather Service Fairbanks AK

258 PM AKDT Fri Aug 8 2025



.DISCUSSION...

Cooler weather today as troughing grows over the state following

a ridge that has now been pushed off to the east. Widespread and

numerous showers continue to creep in from the west this afternoon

to the central Interior, reaching the eastern Interior starting

Saturday night. These showers are likely to bring wetting rains to

much of the region, keeping min RH values mostly above 50%, 

except for the Upper Tanana Valley where rain chances remain low 

until Sunday. Isolated thunderstorms are possible in the 

central/eastern Interior Saturday afternoon and continue to shift 

eastward in to mainly the eastern Interior by Sunday afternoon. 

Thunderstorms are not expected going into Monday. Temperatures 

will cool in the upper 50s/low 60s through the weekend, with a 

brief period of warming Tuesday and Wednesday before another 

cooling trend sets in. Winds will be mainly out of the southeast 

before shifting towards the southwest Saturday afternoon. Winds 

speeds will be light for most of the period, but are expected to 

strengthen going into Sunday ahead of the pattern shift. 



