FXUS64 KLZK 082301 AAA

AFDLZK



Area Forecast Discussion...UPDATED

National Weather Service Little Rock AR

601 PM CDT Fri Aug 8 2025



...New AVIATION...



.DISCUSSION...

Issued at 110 AM CDT Fri Aug 8 2025



Mainly quiet conditions are ongoing across the state early this Fri 

morning. However...some patchy/isolated pockets of rain were noted 

dropping south over ERN and even portions of central AR. This 

activity is result of a very weak upper wave diving south around the 

ERN periphery of the upper ridge to the west. Expect this potential 

for some very isolated SHRA to continue into the early morning 

hrs...with some slight chance POPs mentioned as a result. 



Another weak upper wave may dive south along the MS River this Fri 

afternoon...which could trigger more isolated convection this 

afternoon. However..this activity should remain mostly east of the 

CWA...keeping silent POPs due to the fairly low confidence. 

Otherwise...expecting another typical summer day this Fri...with 

temps around or just above normal. Dewpts may mix out enough to keep 

most areas just below Heat Adv criteria. However...keep the same 

areal coverage of current Heat Adv for WRN sections along the AR 

River Valley as this area has best potential for seeing heat index 

values exceeding 105 this afternoon. This may be a repeat for Sat as 

well. 



The upper ridge centered to the west of AR late this week will 

gradually weaken and shift further west over the weekend...with 

chances for convection increasing slightly as weak low pressure to 

the SE moves closer to AR. By the early to middle part of next 

week...AR and the Mid-South will be under a weak upper trough...with 

chances for afternoon diurnally driven convection increasing as a 

result. Temps will cool slightly also for highs...but low level 

moisture levels look to also increase some. This may keep heat index 

values elevated around 100 each afternoon. Otherwise...no major 

systems or fronts will bring organized convection through the end of 

the forecast...just more isolated to widely scattered afternoon 

convection possible each day. &&



