043

FNUS76 KMTR 082301

FWSMTR



Spot Forecast for BERRY...CAL FIRE

National Weather Service San Francisco CA

401 PM PDT Fri Aug 8 2025



Forecast is based on forecast start time of 0700 PDT on August 09. 

If conditions become unrepresentative, contact the National Weather

Service.



.DISCUSSION...Hot and dry conditions continue through the

beginning of next week with very poor humidity retention during

the daytime. Breezy southerly winds are expected to develop 

during each afternoon and evening, which could bring moisture 

from Lake Berryessa to the forecast site. If winds take a more 

southwesterly direction, then local terrain could result in 

locally warmer temperatures at the site. A slight cooling trend

will begin on Tuesday.



.SATURDAY...



Sky/weather.........Sunny. 

Max temperature.....94-104. 

Min humidity........14-25 percent. 

Wind (20 ft)........South winds 5 to 15 mph. 

CWR.................0 percent. 

Chance of thunder...0 percent. 

Mixing height.......7800 ft AGL. 

Transport winds.....Southwest around 7 mph. 

Marine layer........None. 



.SATURDAY NIGHT...



Sky/weather.........Clear. 

Min temperature.....62-66. 

Max humidity........65-70 percent. 

Wind (20 ft)........South winds 5 to 14 mph in the evening 

                    becoming light. 

CWR.................0 percent. 

Chance of thunder...0 percent. 

Mixing height.......900 ft AGL. 

Transport winds.....West around 9 mph. 

Marine layer........None. 



$$

