064

FXUS64 KBRO 082302 AAB

AFDBRO



Area Forecast Discussion...UPDATED

National Weather Service Brownsville TX

602 PM CDT Fri Aug 8 2025



...New AVIATION...



.DISCUSSION...

Issued at 1206 PM CDT Fri Aug 8 2025



Typical summertime hot and humid conditions are expected to persist 

over Deep South Texas as upper-level ridging continues both over the 

desert Southwest and the over the Eastern Gulf. At the surface, mild 

offshore troughing will create conditions that are conducive for sea 

breeze shower/thunderstorm formation tomorrow through midweek next 

week. Isolated showers and thunderstorms are expected to form mainly 

in the afternoons as the sea breeze surges westward inland, and are 

expected primarily in areas east of I-69C. Chances of precipitation 

each day will range between 20-30%. Winds will be light to moderate 

and south-southeasterly, allowing for continual advection of Gulf 

moisture throughout the week.  



Heat risk is also a concern throughout the forecast period, as 

temperatures are expected to climb into the upper 90s/lower 100s 

every day this weekend into next week.  In addition, heat indices 

will be even higher due to humidity, with values slowly increasing 

through the end of next week.  Moderate heat risk (level 2 of 4) is 

expected throughout Deep South Texas this weekend into early next 

week and will increase to a Major Heat Risk (level 3 of 4) by the 

middle of next week. When this occurs, Special Weather Statements or 

Heat Advisories may become necessary. Low temperatures will be in 

the upper 70s and even the lower 80s for portions of the Lower Rio 

Grande Valley.



&&



.AVIATION...

(00Z TAFS)

Issued at 600 PM CDT Fri Aug 8 2025



VFR conditions are expected through the TAF period. Moderate 

southeasterly winds will become light this evening into the 

overnight.



&&



.MARINE...

Issued at 1206 PM CDT Fri Aug 8 2025



Favorable marine conditions are expected throughout this weekend 

into next week with low wave heights (between 1-3 feet) and gentle 

to moderate south-southeasterly winds. Wind speeds should remain 

below Small Craft Advisory and Small Craft Exercise Caution 

criteria throughout the week. There is a small (up to 20%) chance 

of some isolated showers/thunderstorms over the Gulf waters and 

the Bay throughout the week. 



&&



