=================================================



129

FXUS63 KPAH 082306

AFDPAH



Area Forecast Discussion

National Weather Service Paducah KY

606 PM CDT Fri Aug 8 2025



.KEY MESSAGES...



- Typical summer-time heat and humidity will continue through

  the next 7 days. Daily highs are forecast to be in the upper

  80s to lower 90s with heat index readings making it "feel

  like" 95 to 100 degrees.



- Outside of a few isolated showers this afternoon, dry weather

  is forecast through the weekend. Low chances (30-40%) of 

  showers and storms return on a near daily basis next week, 

  peaking each afternoon.



&&



.UPDATE...

Issued at 601 PM CDT Fri Aug 8 2025



Updated Aviation discussion for 00Z TAF Issuance.



&&



.DISCUSSION...

Issued at 211 PM CDT Fri Aug 8 2025



500 mb ridging will continue to build over much of the eastern 

CONUS through much of the weekend as it very gradually drifts east. 

At the same time, a wrapped up upper-level low will shift eastward 

through the Canadian Prairies. Between these two features will be 

the main focus for multiple storm complexes through the weekend into 

next week as they focus along a cold front drifting gradually 

southeastward. As the front drifts closer to the area early next 

week, expect a better chance for at least scattered afternoon 

showers and thunderstorms to develop. Additional deep-layer moisture 

is also progged to lift northward from the Gulf through mid week. 

Temperatures will be in the upper 80s to low 90s. The increasing 

moisture levels will also make if feel less comfortable outside with 

afternoon heat index values pushing closer to the mid 90s.



The ridge is still expected to amplify once again for the end of the 

week into next weekend, pushing high temperatures up toward the mid 

90s with heat index values approaching 100 degrees.



&&



.AVIATION /00Z TAFS THROUGH 00Z SATURDAY/...

Issued at 601 PM CDT Fri Aug 8 2025



A high pressure dominated forecast means Visual Flight Rules

conditions with daily diurnal cu offering bases generally in the

4-6K FT AGL range over the course of the day. If there are any

restrictions, it would be in the form of daybreak or predawn 

fog, but modeled TDD's do not suggest this being a big impact, 

so we've refrained from its mention this issuance. 



&&



.PAH WATCHES/WARNINGS/ADVISORIES...

IL...None.

MO...None.

IN...None.

KY...None.



&&



$$



