175

FXUS64 KSJT 082309

AFDSJT



Area Forecast Discussion

National Weather Service San Angelo TX

609 PM CDT Fri Aug 8 2025



...New AVIATION...



.KEY MESSAGES...



- Heat Advisory in effect for the Big Country through 8 PM.



- Hot and dry conditions through this weekend.



- Not quite as hot for Monday and Tuesday with a few widely

  scattered showers and storms possible.



&&



.SHORT TERM...

(This evening through Saturday)

Issued at 1234 PM CDT Fri Aug 8 2025



The upper level ridge will remain in control of the weather in

west central Texas through Saturday. A Heat Advisory will remain

in effect for the Big Country through 8 PM tonight for 

temperatures and heat index values around 105 degrees. Somewhat

breezy south winds will persist through the early evening before

diminishing to 5 to 10 mph out of the south/southeast tonight.

Lows will be in the 70s. On Saturday, temperatures are expected to

cool just slightly, with highs topping out in the upper 90s along

the I-10 corridor to near 104 degrees in the western Big Country.

Heat Index values should max out near 102 degrees. Although it 

will still be hot, it looks like any Heat Advisory readings will 

be isolated, so will hold off on issuing a Heat Advisory for now. 



&&



.LONG TERM...

(Saturday night through next Friday)

Issued at 1234 PM CDT Fri Aug 8 2025



For Sunday, looks hot and dry across the area but temperatures a 

few degrees cooler than Saturday. Highs will be in the mid 90s to 

around 102. Please follow heat safety precautions. The upper level

ridge will break down early next week and a surge of tropical 

moisture will result in cooler temperatures for much of next week.

Highs will be in the upper 80s and 90s, but will mainly stay 

below 100. However, expect humid conditions due to dewpoints 

remaining in the 60s to lower 70s. Also, and easterly wave will 

bring low chances of rain/a few thunderstorms to much of the area 

Monday and Tuesday. The activity will be isolated to widely 

scattered and most areas will not probably not see any rainfall. 

The best potential for brief torrential rainfall will be across 

the Heartland and Northwest Hill Country Tuesday afternoon.



&&



.AVIATION...

(00Z TAFS)

Issued at 608 PM CDT Fri Aug 8 2025



VFR conditions will continue across West Central Texas terminals

through Saturday afternoon. South to southeast winds will prevail

and will continue to be gusty at times, especaily during daylight

hours.



&&



.PRELIMINARY POINT TEMPS/POPS...

Abilene     76 102  76  99 /   0   0   0   0 

San Angelo  73 100  73  98 /   0   0   0   0 

Junction    71  99  69  96 /   0   0   0   0 

Brownwood   73  99  73  96 /   0   0   0   0 

Sweetwater  77 103  76 101 /   0   0   0   0 

Ozona       72  98  71  97 /   0   0   0   0 

Brady       73  96  72  93 /   0   0   0   0 



&&



.SJT WATCHES/WARNINGS/ADVISORIES...

Heat Advisory until 8 PM CDT this evening for Callahan-Fisher-

Haskell-Jones-Nolan-Shackelford-Taylor-Throckmorton.



&&



$$



