Albuquerque Aviation Discussion

Issued at 1919 UTC Friday, August  8, 2025



.AVIATION...

(18Z TAFS)

Issued at 115 PM MDT Fri Aug 8 2025

VFR conditions are expected to prevail throughout the TAF period at 

all terminals. Isolated showers and thunderstorms are expected to 

develop after 20z, with a main threat of gusty outflow winds. 

PROB30s are in place across central terminals more likely to see 

these outflow winds. Gusty west winds are also expected across 

western NM affecting KGUP and more so KFMN. A stray strong to 

isolated severe storm may develop across northeast NM near KRTN to 

KCAO, with damaging wind gusts and hail. After 03z tonight, a low 

level jet kicks in across eastern NM, inducing LLWS at KTCC around 

06z. There are lower chances of LLWS at KROW, but not enough 

confidence to put in the TAF. Isolated instances of LLWS may occur 

at KFMN during the same time frame.



