533

FXUS63 KUNR 082316

AFDUNR



Area Forecast Discussion For Western SD and Northeastern WY

National Weather Service Rapid City SD

516 PM MDT Fri Aug 8 2025



.KEY MESSAGES...



-  Marginal (level 1 of 5) risk of severe thunderstorms late this

   afternoon/evening.



- Dry pattern expected throughout the weekend and into next week.



- Seasonal temperatures expected.



&&



.DISCUSSION...(This Evening Through Friday)

Issued at 115 PM MDT Fri Aug 8 2025



A cold front has pushed through all of western SD late this

morning and in its wake a cooler and drier airmass has advected

into the region. Water vapor and VIS shows a broad closed low

spinning across northeastern Montana with a clear defined dry slot

wrapping up near the center. This dry slot is rapidly moving

eastward and will bring drier air to much of the region tonight.

With clearing skies, weakening winds and the drier and cool air

advection lows tonight across the Black Hills could drop into the

40s in some locations. As the main area of low pressure/trough

approaches the area some residual CAPE values around 1000 J/kg are

hanging around the plains and points east. With large amounts of

shear, any storms that do initiate could pose a small window of a

severe threat although CAMS and Hi-RES models don't seem to

excited about CI (Convective Initiation) this afternoon and even 

the Storm Prediction Center has pulled the Marginal Risk almost 

completely out of our area for this afternoon and evening.



Heading into the weekend, the pattern begins to shift toward a

prolonged period of dry weather with temperatures warming to

seasonal as the winds aloft switch from the Northwest to the

southwest as upper level ridging begins to build across much of

the western CONUS. Predominately dry conditions with gradual

warming temperatures can be expected through much of next week.

Some diurnal low end PoP chances will be possible by midweek.



&&



.AVIATION...(For the 00Z TAFS Through 00Z Saturday Evening)

Issued At 514 PM MDT Fri Aug 8 2025



Isold TS are possible through 09/02Z across the nrn Black Hills

and down near KIEN. Brief gusty winds are possible with some of

the stronger storms as they pass through. Otw VFR conds are

expected through the valid fcst period. 



&&



.UNR WATCHES/WARNINGS/ADVISORIES...

SD...None.

WY...None.

&&



$$



DISCUSSION/KEY MESSAGES...Woodward

AVIATION...Hintz



