Forecast is based on forecast start time of 0800 PDT on August 09. 

If conditions become unrepresentative, contact the National Weather

Service.



...HEAT ADVISORY IN EFFECT UNTIL 8 PM PDT MONDAY...



.DISCUSSION...



Currently, temperatures are in the mid-90s with humidity slowly 

increasing to 20-25% and WSW winds 10-15 mph gusting to 25 mph.

Winds will remain elevated in the next few hours then become light

and variable overnight with humidity recovering to 40-45% by

Saturday morning.



Winds will initially pick up out of the NE at 10 mph in the 

morning, then switch to WSW 10-15 mph, gusting to 20-25 mph 

between 2-4 PM. Temperatures will peak in the low to mid-90s and 

humidity will fall to around 20%. Winds will ease slowly after

10PM Saturday and become light and variable overnight. Relative 

humidity will peak around 45-50% early Sunday. Expect similar

temperatures, humidity and west winds Sunday afternoon.









