FWFAER



FIRE WEATHER PLANNING FORECAST FOR SOUTHCENTRAL ALASKA

NATIONAL WEATHER SERVICE ANCHORAGE AK

324 PM AKDT Fri Aug 8 2025



.DISCUSSION...



Scattered wetting rainfall continues across Southcentral Alaska 

this afternoon. Breaks in cloud cover may allow for brief 

thunder in the Susitna Valley due to instability. Saturday will 

have another round of wetting rains due to a front. Parts of the 

Susitna Valley including Talkeetna may see thunderstorms before 

the bulk of the rainfall arrives in the evening. The Copper River 

Basin will be drier with periods of sunshine. Sunday sees more 

rainfall with the Copper River Basin from Gulkana north having 

thunderstorm chances due to higher instability. The Talkeetna

Mountains and parts of the Susitna Valley from Talkeetna north

will also have chances for thunderstorms. Monday will see a drying

trend as a ridge moves in. Winds will be relatively light apart

from the Copper River Basin which will see breezy SE winds.



