[{"xmlns":"nwws-oi","id":"nwws_processor.8731","issue":"2025-08-08T23:29:00Z","ttaaii":"FXUS64","cccc":"KMRX","awipsid":"AFDMRX"}]
=================================================



850

FXUS64 KMRX 082329

AFDMRX



Area Forecast Discussion

National Weather Service Morristown TN

729 PM EDT Fri Aug 8 2025



...New AVIATION...



.DISCUSSION...

Issued at 1238 PM EDT Fri Aug 8 2025



Key Messages: 



1. Isolated to showers and thunderstorms will affect a few spots 

over the weekend especially the higher terrain, then rain chances

will increase for next week.



2. Temperatures will generally be around seasonal normals.



Discussion:



The weak upper trough that has been over our area will give way to 

upper ridging for the weekend into early next week.  Limited 

moisture and instability will keep afternoon convection coverage 

mainly isolated and more likely to occur over the higher terrain 

during the weekend. 



A more southerly component to the low level flow will allow for an 

increase in moisture next week, along with an increase in diurnally 

driven showers and thunderstorms. By mid-week models are generally 

showing some short wave energy affecting our region while an upper 

trough moves across southern Canada and the Great Lakes, temporarily 

suppressing the ridge. This would lead to more coverage of 

convection during the Tuesday/Wednesday/Thursday time frame, 

although timing is uncertain. Behind this short wave, upper ridging 

will reassert dominance over the region, although chances for mostly 

diurnal showers and storms will continue Friday.  



Temperatures will be a bit higher than recent days for the upcoming 

weekend through the bulk of the work week, but will generally not

be far from seasonal normals. 

  



&&



.AVIATION...

(00Z TAFS)

Issued at 722 PM EDT Fri Aug 8 2025



Isolated showers will dissipate over the next few hours. Some MVFR

CIGs are possible in the morning hours especially near CHA where 

it rained but confidence is low. Tomorrow afternoon showers and

storms will be isolated with very low chances at each terminal.



&&



