Area Forecast Discussion

National Weather Service Corpus Christi TX

636 PM CDT Fri Aug 8 2025



...New AVIATION...



.KEY MESSAGES...

Updated at 629 PM CDT Fri Aug 8 2025



- Generally low to medium 20-45% chances of showers and 

thunderstorms over the weekend and into early next week.



- Generally minor to moderate risk of heat related impacts across 

most of South Texas. At times, a brief major risk can be expected 

across portions of the Brush Country, through the period. 



- Elevated fire weather conditions across the southwestern portions 

of Webb County through the weekend and into next week.



&&



.DISCUSSION...

Issued at 1233 PM CDT Fri Aug 8 2025



A mid and upper level high pressure system remains dominate across S 

TX, keeping rain chances low (10-20) tonight through Saturday, as 

well as hot with afternoon heat indices generally ranging from 100-

109. A few areas could briefly reach around 110 as the sea breeze 

moves inland each afternoon, but conditions should remain below Heat 

Advisory levels due to it being localized and brief. Generally there 

is minor to moderate risk of heat related impacts each day with a 

few locations across the Brush Country briefly reaching major risk 

through the period.



The high will shift northwest Sunday as an inverted trough 

approaches S TX from the gulf. This will bring slightly deeper 

moisture along with upper support and will combine with the sea 

breeze to produce more areal coverage of showers and thunderstorms. 

Rain chances will be low to medium (20-40%)by Sunday and continues 

through Tuesday. Ridge builds across the area as the trough exits to 

the west. Thus, decreasing rain chances to 10-20% by the middle of 

next week.



Elevated fire weather conditions may exist across southwestern 

portions of Webb County due to minimum RH values forecast to be 25-

30 percent and above normal Energy Release Component values. 

However, winds are expected to remain below thresholds.



&&



.AVIATION...

(00Z TAFS)

Issued at 629 PM CDT Fri Aug 8 2025



VFR conditions will prevail across South Texas through tomorrow

afternoon, with brief MVFR vsby and cigs over the inland Coastal

Plains from 10-14Z, impacting ALI/VCT. Persistent pattern with

weak winds, only gusting to around 20 knots in the wake of the

seabreeze.



&&



.MARINE...

Issued at 1233 PM CDT Fri Aug 8 2025



A generally light to gentle (BF 2-3) south to southeast flow is 

expected through the period. Bays south of Port Aransas, will 

increase to a gentle to moderate (BF 3-4) breeze in the afternoons 

and evenings. There is 10-30 percent chance of showers and 

thunderstorms Saturday, mainly offshore. Chances increase to a 20-50 

percent Sunday, then decrease to 15-40 percent next week.



