Riverton Aviation Discussion

Issued at 2159 UTC Friday, August  8, 2025



.AVIATION /00Z TAFS THROUGH 00Z SATURDAY/...

Issued at 358 PM MDT Fri Aug 8 2025

Gusty winds will diminishing towards sunset. Mostly clear skies and 

light winds (less than 10 kts) will prevail overnight at all 

terminals. A shortwave will push some FL150-FL200 CIGs back into the 

region Saturday morning, but no precipitation is expected. Winds 

will start to increase towards 18/19Z Saturday across southwest WY, 

but will be much less than today with gusts staying under 20kts into 

Saturday afternoon. 

Please see the Aviation Weather Center and/or CWSU ZDV and ZLC for 

the latest information on smoke, icing, and turbulence

forecasts.



Cheyenne Aviation Discussion

Issued at 2141 UTC Friday, August  8, 2025



.AVIATION /18Z TAFS THROUGH 18Z SATURDAY/...

Issued at 1137 AM MDT Fri Aug 8 2025

VFR conditions expected over the next 24 hours. Winds breezy

from a westerly to a northwesterly direction, gusts 20-30 knots.

A chance of passing showers or storms this evening primarily

impacting Nebraska terminals, with any precipitation causing

possible higher winds that will be erratic. Cloud decks staying

mostly mid height, around 5-10k feet, lifting and clearing 

overnight into tomorrow with the most likely place for lingering

clouds NE terminals.





